+<frozen-after-approval reason="human-owned intent — do not modify unless human renegotiates">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** 70 Meadowgate converts 11% of invited enquirers to completed applications; PostHog cannot see submissions, section drop-off, returning visitors, or email opens/clicks, and the invite/reminder/form-header copy promises "a few minutes" against a form demanding ~21 mandatory inputs incl. two third-party letters (the measured top abandonment drivers).
+
+**Approach:** Ship the merged report's Wave 0 instrumentation pack (consent-gated funnel events on the /apply pages, stable per-vacancy anonymous id, Resend tags + UTM + domain-tracking runbook) and Wave 1a copy pack (honest "what you'll need" checklist in invite/auto-reply/form header, two-stage doc-gathering reminder series with send machinery, kill every "few minutes / 10 minutes" lie). Stepper (F1) and save-resume (F3) are separate jobs — copy must not promise save-and-continue.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Client analytics honor the existing consent gate: nothing captured/persisted unless analytics consent granted (same posture as current `$pageview`); no PII (emails, names, values) in any event — field KEYS only.
+- Keep `person_profiles: 'identified_only'`, `opt_out_capturing_by_default: true`, `/_ph` proxy, and the `rt:consent-changed` opt-in/out listener semantics.
+- No-JS path untouched: one long SSR form, one POST; events are progressive enhancement.
+- Brand voice: calm, no exclamation marks, honest specifics; property-name-first email subjects (mobile truncation).
+- Spam (honeypot/timing) fake-confirmation must NOT fire the confirmation event; duplicate page is a distinct event; validation-error re-render is a distinct event.
+- Migration FILES may be added; run them only against the local docker test DB (`make test-db-up`). Never staging/prod. Never commit `.env`.
+- One-shot reminder stays atomic + self-healing (failed send clears its stamp); Resend batch send (5/batch, 1.1 s pause) reused for stage 2.
+
+**Ask First:** enabling Resend open/click tracking on the production domain (DNS CNAME + dashboard/API change — documented for Moses, NOT done by us); anything touching prod DB.
+
+**Never:** build F1 stepper or F3 save-resume; promise "save and continue later" in copy; change mandatory-letter requirements (Q6 lock); weaken spam/validation guards; change `person_profiles` or consent defaults; server-side capture of applicant behavior (consent-free measurement is the DB cohort rate, already available).
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Successful submit | POST valid | confirmation page `data-apply-page="confirmation"` → `application_confirmation_viewed` (queued until consent) | n/a |
+| Validation fail | POST invalid | `data-apply-page="form-errors"` → `application_submit_failed` {error_count, first_error_field}; NO confirmation event; NO section tracking on this render | n/a |
+| Spam submit | honeypot/timing | fake confirmation WITHOUT event marker → no event | n/a |
+| Duplicate submit | same email twice | duplicate page → `application_duplicate_viewed` | n/a |
+| Consent rejected/absent | banner reject or ignore | events queue in-memory, dropped on pagehide; anon id NOT persisted (fresh random per load, inert under opt-out) | no-op, no throw |
+| Consent granted mid-visit | click Accept | queued events flush; anon id persisted to localStorage; stable across reloads | storage failure → in-memory only |
+| Consent withdrawn | reject after accept | posthog.reset (existing) + stored anon id removed | n/a |
+| Section funnel | scroll form | `section_entered` once/section/pageview (IntersectionObserver); `section_completed` when all visible required fields filled (radio groups by name, hidden `[data-condition]`/co-applicant cards excluded); `section_abandoned` on pagehide/visibilitychange for deepest entered-incomplete section | no IO → no entered events, no crash; submit → no abandoned |
+| Error re-render scroll | form-errors page | no section events (keeps funnel to pristine GET pageviews) | n/a |
+| Remind click, mixed pool | 3 never-reminded, 5 reminded ≥2 days ago | stage-1 email ×3, stage-2 email ×5, response {reminded:3, followup:5} | per-send failure clears matching stamp |
+| Remind click, all reminded <2 days ago | followup_count=0 | button disabled "Everyone reminded"; handler sends nothing | n/a |
+| No posthog key / ad-blocked | key="" | pages render identically; apply_analytics.js no-ops | silent |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
