+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given a consenting visitor, when they submit successfully, then exactly one `application_confirmation_viewed` fires with `{vacancy_short_code}` and no confirmation event fires on spam/duplicate/error renders.
+- Given no consent, when any /apply page loads, then zero events leave the browser and no anon id persists across reloads; given consent, the id survives reloads per vacancy.
+- Given a consenting visitor scrolling the pristine form, then per pageview each section emits at most one entered/completed, and leaving mid-form emits one abandoned for the deepest incomplete section.
+- Given the new templates, when `rg -i "few minutes|takes about 10 minutes"` runs over `server/src client/src`, then zero applicant-promise hits remain (only unrelated justified hits: AI-analysis timing, rate-limit waits).
+- Given invite/auto-reply/reminder emails, then each carries Resend tags (`template`, `vacancy_id`) and a UTM-tagged apply link, and names both letters + ~15 min + one-visit up front.
+- Given a vacancy with mixed reminder states, when the landlord clicks the button once, then each enquirer gets the correct stage and stamps/counts/labels reflect both stages.
+- `make test` (shared+client+server incl. `test-js`) green; integration tests green against docker test DB.
