+## Design Notes
+
+- Consent-gated capture helper (apply_analytics.js core, exported for node tests): `capture(name, props)` → if `posthog.__loaded && has_opted_in_capturing()` send; else queue; one `rt:consent-changed` listener flushes on `detail.analytics===true`, drops on false. Queue is per-pageview memory only — deliberate: matches "floor, not total" posture, nothing stored pre-consent.
+- Stable id: key `rt_apply_did:<short_code>`; read at snippet time (fallback random `applicant-<code>-<rand>`); written ONLY inside the grant branch (`posthog.get_distinct_id()`), removed on withdrawal. Keeps per-vacancy cohorting (no cross-vacancy identity) and the current pre-consent posture.
+- Page disambiguation is server-rendered `data-apply-page` on `<body>` — the POST-response-without-redirect pattern makes URL-based reads ambiguous, the marker is not.
+- F3 seam: prep block carries a code comment `F3-SEAM` — when save-resume ships, swap the "one visit" line for "save and continue later"; stage-2 reminder CTA is the apply URL today, becomes the continue-link when F3 exists (single `application_url` param).
+- Resend open/click tracking is domain-level (Resend docs, verified 2026-07): enabling it on the prod domain + CNAME is a Moses runbook step in the PR; tags make opens/clicks sliceable by template/stage once enabled, UTM gives PostHog-side click measurement immediately.
+- Section "completed": all VISIBLE `[required]` controls non-empty (radios grouped by name; checkboxes checked; files/selects/text non-empty), visibility = not inside `[hidden]` (form.js toggles `hidden` on data-condition wrappers and required on employer blocks); section with zero visible-required (tell_us_more) completes on any interaction. Debounced ~400 ms re-check on input/change.
