+---   - every inbound row has a stage-1 stamp (a fresh un-reminded re-enquiry
+---     restarts the series — stage 1 goes to them in the same click)
+---   - the most recent stage-1 stamp is at least 2 days old (prevents an
+---     accidental same-session double-send of both stages; the actual
+---     cadence is the landlord's click)
+---   - no stage-2 stamp NEWER than the latest stage-1 (a stage-2 from a
+---     previous enquiry cycle must not block a restarted series)
+--- and the vacancy itself has not passed its closing date (a deadline email
+--- announcing a past date is worse than none). Consuming the one-shot in the
+--- same statement makes a double-click safe: the second call matches zero
+--- rows. All of the enquirer's rows are stamped so the DISTINCT-ON-latest
+--- awaiting list always displays the flag. Recipients are deduped
+--- (case-folded) and validated in Gleam before send.
+UPDATE inbound_email
+SET second_reminder_sent_at = now()
+WHERE vacancy_id = $1
+  AND second_reminder_sent_at IS NULL
+  AND sender_email IS NOT NULL
+  AND sender_email <> ''
+  AND lower(sender_email) IN (
+    SELECT sender_email_lc
+    FROM inbound_email_sender_state
+    WHERE vacancy_id = $1
+      AND NOT has_unreminded
+      AND last_stage1_at < now() - interval '2 days'
+      AND (last_stage2_at IS NULL OR last_stage2_at <= last_stage1_at)
+  )
+  AND (SELECT closes_at FROM vacancy WHERE id = $1) > now()
+RETURNING sender_email, sender_name
